      "source_page_number": null,
      "source_image_index": null,
      "ownership": "unknown"
    },
    "parts": [],
    "answer_text": "The Indian Peninsula drifted towards the north and finally collided with the much larger Eurasian Plate. As a result of this collision, the sedimentary rocks which were accumulated in the geosynclines (known as Tethys) got folded and formed the mountain systems of the West Asia and Himalaya.",
    "answer_latex": null,
    "steps": [],
    "final_answer": "Thus, the Himalayas were formed due to the collision of the Indian Peninsula with the Eurasian Plate.",
